  <issue>
  Edit last message keyboard shortcut (←) may unexpectedly mark many messages read
If you write a message in a narrowed view, then go back to an unnarrowed view, there may now be many unread messages between your new current position and the message you just wrote. If you then accidentally press `←`, all of those messages will be marked read unexpectedly, causing you to lose your place while catching up.

We should either
* disable the `←` shortcut if there are unread messages between your current position and the message to be edited, or
* disable the `←` shortcut if you’ve switched views since writing the last message.
  </issue>
  
